 The Svedberg equation is given by:  
$$
s = \frac{M(1 - \nu \rho)}{N_A R T \nu}
$$  
Where:  
- $s$ is the sedimentation coefficient ($2.02 \times 10^{-13} \, \text{sec}$)  
- $M$ is the molecular weight (g/mol)  
- $\nu$ is the partial specific volume ($0.707 \, \text{cm}^3/\text{g}$)  
- $\rho$ is the density of water ($0.998 \, \text{g/cm}^3$)  
- $N_A$ is Avogadro's number ($6.022 \times 10^{23} \, \text{mol}^{-1}$)  
- $R$ is the gas constant ($8.314 \, \text{J/(mol·K)}$)  
